{"id": "sdqa0088", "pool": "sdqa", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 4.16, "n_chunks": 5, "n_concurrent": 5, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.1712, "eot_read_ms": 18, "reference_answer": "a phenomenon often attributed as a form of gender-based price discrimination", "query": "What is the pink tax?", "transcript": "What is the Pink Tax?", "mode": "local", "answer": "Once upon a time, in a quiet valley beside a slow green river, lived a small dragon named Ember. Every morning, Ember would wake up to the gentle chirping of birds and the soft rustle of leaves. Instead of fiery breath, Ember had a tiny puff of sparkles that made flowers bloom wherever he went. The villagers loved him dearly, bringing him berries and stories of faraway lands. One day, a thick fog rolled in, hiding the path to the village. Without hesitation, Ember used his sparkles to light the way, guiding everyone safely home. From that day on, the legend of the gentle dragon who lit the path spread across the valley, reminding everyone that even the smallest hearts can make the biggest difference.", "answer_ms": 3144}
