{"id": "sdqa0136", "pool": "sdqa", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 2.96, "n_chunks": 3, "n_concurrent": 3, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.4486, "eot_read_ms": 18, "reference_answer": "Luis von Ahn, David Abraham, Manuel Blum, Michael Crawford, Ben Maurer, Colin McMillen, and Edison Tan", "query": "Who developed Recaptcha?", "transcript": "Who developed recapture?", "mode": "local", "answer": "The reCAPTCHA system was developed by Google. It was created to help distinguish between human and automated interactions on websites, primarily to prevent spam and abuse. The name \"reCAPTCHA\" comes from \"recaptcha,\" a type of challenge-response test where users are asked to identify distorted text or perform tasks that are easy for humans but difficult for computers. Over time, the technology has evolved, incorporating more advanced techniques like machine learning to improve its effectiveness and reduce reliance on visual challenges.", "answer_ms": 2012}
{"id": "sdqa0139", "pool": "sdqa", "tier": "balanced", "audio_s": 6.66, "n_chunks": 7, "n_concurrent": 7, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.509, "eot_read_ms": 18, "reference_answer": "Germany", "query": "Where was the first sex change operation performed?", "transcript": "Where was the first sex change operation performed?", "mode": "escalated", "relay": "The first widely documented gender-affirming \"sex change\" surgeries were performed in Germany, notably in Berlin at Magnus Hirschfeld’s Institute for Sexual Science in the early 1930s. If referring to Lili Elbe, her operations were performed in Germany, including at a clinic in Dresden.", "expert_answer": "The first widely documented gender-affirming “sex change” surgeries were performed in **Germany**, notably in **Berlin** at Magnus Hirschfeld’s Institute for Sexual Science in the early 1930s.  \n\nIf referring to **Lili Elbe**, her operations were performed in **Germany**, including at a clinic in **Dresden**.", "expert_latency_s": 6.36, "stall_ms": 21, "relay_ms": 1301}
